Z||000014||dman||07-27-2000||03:09 PM||||That car was in the Knotts Fun in the Sun show this past April. I saw it first hand, I probably even took a pic of it (I took a lot of pics when I was there).<P>From someone who has seen it firsthand -- It looks good. Very good.<P>Yeah it only has the stock v6, and yeah its an automatic, and yeah 44 grand is a lot of money. But like rockcrawl said, "Everyone, young or old, will turn their head to get a second look at a Diablo"<P> Personally, I'd prefer a Ferrari or a GT40, but I can still appreciate the beauty of this Diablo. But for 44 grand there had better be a cupholder there somewhere!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000015||Raydar||07-28-2000||11:37 AM||||If I were so inclined...<BR>I'd just go with the Artero kit from Pisa.<BR>The kit is about $5K. Fits on a stock space-frame. <BR>Causes pedestrian whiplash on a grand scale.<BR>One of the guys in our club built this one, based on an 86 SE. The pic <I>doesn't</I> do it justice. It's absolutely flawless.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Craig1.jpg">  <BR> <P>------------------<BR><BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO 3800)<P>"Some mornings, it just isn't worth<BR>chewing through the restraints."||||reg||1
Z||000016||b lo 0||07-28-2000||11:53 AM||||A company builds a Diablo kit that fits on a standard Fiero frame for about $3-4,000.  Looks absolutely indistiguishable from a full-length Lambo.  It's available in standard and the 2000 VT-a la Removable Roof (same price-hmmmm, i wonder which one...).  The kit even comes with the replica wheels!!!  Great looking kit, great sounding price.  I'll give yall a heads up on the company.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">  <BR>Go to <A HREF="http://www.audioimagery.i-p.com" TARGET=_blank>www.audioimagery.i-p.com</A>  !!!||||reg||1
Z||000017||Pontiaddict||07-30-2000||02:52 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Will:<BR><B>He says he stretched it 11 inches. That means there is room for a longitudinal Northstar with Porsche six speed, twin turbochargers, and air/water/freon intercoolers. Can you say 500 RWHP?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually, A twin turbo Northstar makes 600hp without an intercooler. With it, it would kick the crap out of an actual Diablo.(and about anythibg else for that matter.)||||reg||12
Z||000018||Will||07-31-2000||04:49 PM||||They can make 600 HP, but without an intercooler, that's AT LEAST 10 psi of boost after porting and custom fabbed intake and headers. Unless you go for the total rebuild and use 3.4 TDC pistons to frop the static compression into the low 9's (down from 10:1 stock), you'd need some pretty pricey gas to keep away from ping.<BR>     I'd prefer 500 RWHP for 150,000 miles over 600 RWHP for 1,500 miles.<P>     I guess you saw the letter about Northstars in that issue of Hot Rod (Popular Hot Rodding?) some months ago?||||reg||3
